    {"knockout.one_blow", L"A single slap or punch at least this fast knocks a Sim out at once. 0: never in one blow."},
    {"knockout.unconscious", L"On: a knocked-out Sim lies unconscious (Get to Work's collapsed patient: no snoring, no energy change, onlookers react). Off: it falls asleep on the floor (Energy Failure)."},
    {"knockout.minutes", L"How many Sim minutes a knocked-out Sim stays down before it gets up."},
    {"knockout.recover", L"How fast a Sim gets over your blows: its daze halves every this many seconds."},
    {"ragdoll.stagger_omega", L"A staggering Sim is thrown off its feet along the push and comes back; higher = a quicker, shorter stagger."},
    {"ragdoll.stagger_lean", L"How much further the upper body and arms go than the hips when a Sim staggers."},
    {"ragdoll.stagger_step", L"A staggering Sim takes a step when its body is this far from its feet."},
    {"ragdoll.stagger_step_time", L"How long each recovery step of a stagger takes."},
    {"foley.shove", L"An open palm pushed straight into a Sim's chest, back or shoulders makes them stumble or fall back, and they take it as an attack (not the same as shooing a Sim away)."},
    {"foley.shove_speed", L"Your palm must hit at least this fast, straight into them, to count as a shove."},
    {"foley.shove_ratio", L"How much sideways motion a shove allows, as a share of the forward speed. Lower = only straight pushes; higher = swipes count as shoves too."},
    {"foley.shove_force", L"How much of your hand's speed the shoved Sim takes: how far they are thrown back."},
    {"foley.shove_fall_speed", L"A shove at least this fast makes them fall (a ragdoll). Slower shoves make them stumble and recover."},
    {"foley.shove_limp", L"How long a Sim knocked down by a shove lies limp before it blends back to its animation."},
    {"physical.shove_pain", L"How much a shove hurts before speed counts. Higher = more hurt, angry and scared moodlets, more fights."},
    {"physical.friendly_shoves", L"A light shove from a friend (or a playful Sim) counts as play: they laugh, no hurt moodlets."},
    {"foley.knockback", L"A slap or punch knocks the part you hit along the blow and it springs back. 0% none, 200% twice as far."},
    {"foley.rub_speed", L"Sliding your hand along a Sim at least this fast makes rub sounds. 0 turns them off."},
    {"foley.own_sounds", L"Your own sound files (sounds folder: touch, pat, slap, punch, grab) play instead of the game's. A fist (grip + trigger) hitting at punch speed or faster is a punch."},
    {"foley.own_volume", L"How loud all your own touch sounds are (100% = as recorded). The game's touch sounds follow the game's Effects volume."},
    {"foley.volume_touch", L"How loud your own light-touch sounds are."},
    {"foley.volume_pat", L"How loud your own pat sounds are."},
    {"foley.volume_slap", L"How loud your own slap sounds are."},
    {"foley.volume_punch", L"How loud your own punch sounds are (a fist: grip + trigger)."},
    {"foley.volume_grab", L"How loud your own grab sounds are (grip + trigger on their body)."},
    {"foley.knock", L"Make a fist (grip + trigger) and hit a door or window: your own knock sounds (sounds\\knock\\door, sounds\\knock\\window) play where you hit."},
    {"foley.knock_speed", L"A fist slower than this into a door or window makes no knock."},
    {"foley.volume_knock", L"How loud your own knocks are."},
    {"knock.log", L"Write the doors and windows found around you, and each knock, to the log."},
